predictions.grok_explanation:
Democrats won the presidency (Biden) and Senate control (50-50 tie broken by VP Harris) starting Jan 2021, fulfilling the first condition ([Wikipedia: 117th Congress](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/117th_United_States_Congress), [VOA](https://www.voanews.com/a/usa_us-politics_control-white-house-and-congress-democrats-have-2-years-make-big-changes/6201047.html), [Guardian](https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/01/democrats-congress-control-achievements-joe-biden)).

In the first ~2 years (2021-2022), Biden signed substantial legislation:
- American Rescue Plan Act ($1.9T, Mar 2021) ([Wikipedia: Presidency of Joe Biden](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Presidency_of_Joe_Biden), [CNN](https://www.cnn.com/2022/01/20/politics/biden-laws-passed-priorities-to-get-done-executive-orders));
- Infrastructure Investment and Jobs Act ($1.2T, Nov 2021) ([Miller Center](https://millercenter.org/president/biden/key-events));
- CHIPS and Science Act (Aug 2022) ([Miller Center](https://millercenter.org/president/biden/key-events));
- Inflation Reduction Act (Aug 2022), PACT Act, Respect for Marriage Act ([White House](https://bidenwhitehouse.archives.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2025/01/15/the-biden-harris-administration-record/), [NBC News](https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/congress/five-major-bills-congress-passed-2022-rcna61472)).

This matches the prediction of 'substantial volume of legislation'.
